Subject: ARM: dts: bcm2710: name the Morse HAT gpios on Pi 3 / Pi 3 B+

The equivalent change for BCM2711 lives in 991-0005, but the Pi 3 device
trees were never given these names. morse/scripts/chipreset.sh looks the
reset line up with "gpioinfo --by-name MM_RESET" and aborts when it is
absent, so chip reset never worked on a Pi 3.

Pins match the Seeed WM6108 HAT wiring used by the wm6108-spi overlay:
reset GPIO17, wake GPIO23, busy GPIO24.

diff -urN a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts	2026-09-27 08:57:59.037018773 -0500
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts	2026-09-27 08:57:59.039577728 -0500
@@ -46,14 +46,14 @@
 			  "GPIO14",
 			  "GPIO15",
 			  "GPIO16",
-			  "GPIO17",
+			  "MM_RESET",
 			  "GPIO18",
 			  "GPIO19",
 			  "GPIO20",
 			  "GPIO21",
 			  "GPIO22",
-			  "GPIO23",
-			  "GPIO24",
+			  "MM_WAKE",
+			  "MM_BUSY",
 			  "GPIO25",
 			  "GPIO26",
 			  "GPIO27",
diff -urN a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus.dts	2026-09-27 08:57:59.032860523 -0500
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus.dts	2026-09-27 08:57:59.035676530 -0500
@@ -46,14 +46,14 @@
 			  "GPIO14",
